{"step_index":455,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-19T08:44:51Z","input_tokens":2278,"cache_read_tokens":198646,"output_tokens":2122,"thinking":"Considering a fully modular design for the Squad Conclave. This involves a presentation layer focusing on the user interface, a deterministic state engine for calculations, and a pluggable harness for strategies and execution. The proposed architecture will allow for independent modifications and extensions.\n\n\nTwo distinct trading modes are defined: one emulates copy-trading behavior, while the other is a quantitative system using technical analysis. The UI/UX will implement a specific visual aesthetic, including color gradients, glowing indicators, and animated terminal feeds, focusing on the dark cyber Grok Bot style. The codebase will be built using a client-side architecture with specific technologies, prioritizing performance and internal calculations while avoiding external dependencies. Finally, the system will operate within a sandboxed environment, precluding direct access to sensitive financial data or live trading execution, relying instead on a simulation engine.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"CodeContent":"\"# Squad Conclave Deliberation: Grok Bot & Quantitative Trading Architecture\\n\\n- **Date**: 2026-10-19\\n- **Complexity Score**: 5/5 (Multi-domain: System Architecture, UI/UX Craft, Quant Strategy Engine, Hard AppSec/Financial Risk Boundaries)\\n- **Convened Roles**:\\n  - `Blueprint` (Lead Architect & Systems Modularity)\\n  - `Pixel` (UI/UX Craft & Anti-AI Slop Vibecoding)\\n  - `Forge` (Core Engine Implementation & Performance)\\n  - `Shield` (AppSec, Risk Boundaries & Circuit Breakers)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## 1. Input Perspectives\\n\\n### Blueprint (Architecture)\\nThe prompt reveals two distinct trading archetypes that must be unified cleanly:\\n1. **The Grok Bot Social Model (Video 1)**: Copy-trading wallets, 2-L-in-a-row automated firing rule, trader bench rotation, memecoin token stream.\\n2. **The Leaked Quant Model (Image/Prompt)**: Brain vs. Reflex architecture, deterministic state engine (mid, spread, imbalance, volatility), regime classification (`trending`, `mean_reverting`, `high_vol`, `crisis`), and fractional Kelly sizing.\\n\\nWe must build a unified modular architecture where the **Presentation Layer** (Grok Bot dark cyber UI) binds to a **Deterministic Simulation Engine** that supports toggling between **Social Copy-Trading Mode** and **Quant Regime Mode**, with zero dependence on paid third-party proprietary harnesses (`agentkit.xyz`, `typesafe.ai`).\\n\\n### Pixel (UI/UX Craft)\\nThe interface must be a 1:1 homage to the Video 1 Grok Bot aesthetic:\\n- Deep cosmic navy backdrop (`#070913`) with subtle vignette and noise.\\n- Stepped balance history chart rendered on HTML5 Canvas with smooth interpolated transitions and vertical dashed handover flags when traders are fired.\\n- High-contrast glowing stat cards: Balance, Total P&L, Active Trader badge with 6-trade win/loss pills, and Fire Rule indicator.\\n- Live streaming log console with monospace syntax highlighting (`[COPY]`, `[EXIT]`, green profit pills, red loss pills).\\n- Interactive bottom roster carousel showing trader ranking (#1 to #6), win rate, 7-day stats, an\n<truncated 3706 bytes>","Description":"\"Writing Squad Conclave deliberation into decision memory\"","Overwrite":"true","TargetFile":"\"/Users/dev/.gemini/decisions/raw/2026-10-19-trading-bot-architecture.md\"","toolAction":"\"Logging Conclave deliberation\"","toolSummary":"\"Persist Conclave decision file\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
